"duration","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The longest the sequence may go without an element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"throws before the first element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","text":"Example","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["for try await event in serverEvents.timeout(.seconds(30)) {","    handle(event)","}","\/\/ Throws TimeoutError.timedOut if 30 seconds pass without an event"]},{"style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"TimeoutError","typ